# ── Stale ChromaDB segments (only chroma.sqlite3 matters) ────────────────────
data/chroma/
# Stale per-collection UUID segment dirs in data/chroma_db/ (only chroma.sqlite3 is the source of truth)
data/chroma_db/*/

# ── macOS / OS artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Intentionally TRACKED:
# data/ds_wiki.db        — source of truth
# data/rrp/              — RRP bundles
# data/chroma_db/chroma.sqlite3 — ChromaDB index (both machines run bge-large 1024-dim;
#                                 per-collection UUID subdirs are stale segments — gitignored above)
# data/wiki_history.db   — embedding history snapshots
# data/viz/              — visualization outputs
# data/viz_outputs/      — viz runner outputs
# data/reports/          — Fisher Suite HTML reports
# Outside Ref/           — external analysis and reference documents
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Notes on wiki_history.db ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# wiki_history.db IS committed (intentionally tracked, see above) — holds the
# full GSW anchor graph, domain taxonomy, calibration, and embedding snapshots.
# Hysteresis policy in src/snapshot_retention.py keeps it under GitHub's 100MB
# file limit (N=3 snapshots retained; current size ~26MB).
#
# If you clone this repo, the full graph is available immediately via:
#   python3 scripts/gsw_lookup.py "your topic"
#
# The graph is also reproducible from migration scripts in scripts/migrations/
# if the committed DB is ever unavailable.

# ── DB backups (local only; regenerable from migrations or src/sync.py) ──────
data/*.db.bak
data/*.db.pre-*.bak
data/wiki_history.db.*

# ── AlphaEntropy side-project (X8) — separate repo / local only ──────────────
